From e5adf85326d92d3f85187c38fc92e876ff8781b5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 11:22:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 12/13] arm64: dts: qcom: monaco-arduino-monza: keep the RTC
 offset in RTCInfo

The PMM8620AU RTC counter is read-only to the application processor on
the VENTUNO Q (the SPMI arbiter rejects the RTC_RW write with -EPERM),
so the time can only be set as an offset to the counter, and the board
has no nvmem cell for one. The board boots through UEFI firmware, which
keeps the offset in the RTCInfo variable. Describe that, so Linux reads
the time the firmware's SetTime() stored.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Tyler Baker <tyler.baker@oss.qualcomm.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
index d6864a342c58..0fb72d9083c2 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/monaco-arduino-monza.dts
@@ -453,6 +453,10 @@ &pcieport1 {
 	reset-gpios = <&tlmm 23 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
 };
 
+&pmm8620au_0_rtc {
+	qcom,uefi-rtc-info;
+};
+
 &thermal_zones {
 	cpuss-0-0-thermal {
 		polling-delay = <2000>;
-- 
